• The root cause: fixtures/*/tests/ dirs have __init__.py files, making them importable as tests.* packages.
  When pytest collects fixtures/checkout/tests/test_checkout.py it registers the tests namespace. Then when i
  t imports tests/verification/conftest.py it looks for verification.conftest inside the wrong tests package.
   The fix is to add --ignore=fixtures to pytest.ini for the main test suite, but we still need fixture tests
   to run. The cleanest fix is to add testpaths to pytest.ini pointing only at tests/, and separately note th
  at fixture tests run standalone. But the AGENTS.md says python -m pytest -q runs everything.

  The real fix: remove __init__.py from fixtures/*/tests/ so pytest imports them as rootdir-relative paths, n
  ot packages — which is what makes the tests.test_* module name collision happen.
