  ## Tips & Gotchas


  • SQLite on Code Engine: Code Engine scales horizontally; SQLite on a shared PVC works for a single-instanc
  e demo but is not suitable for production multi-instance deployments. For production, migrate ledger.py (or
  chestrator/ledger.py) to use IBM Db2 or PostgreSQL.
  • Docker rehearsal containers: The docker-compose.yml (docker-compose.yml) fixture containers are used by t
  he verification agent at runtime and require Docker-in-Docker, which is not available on Code Engine. The r
  ehearsal agent will degrade gracefully if Docker is unavailable — acceptable for a cloud demo without local
   fixtures.
  • .streamlit/config.toml: This must be present at the working directory root when Streamlit starts, which t
  he Dockerfile.frontend above handles by copying it to /app/.streamlit/.
  • Cold starts: Set --min-scale 1 on both apps to avoid cold-start delays during a live demo.
  • Free tier limits: IBM Cloud Lite accounts have limited Code Engine vCPU-seconds per month. The settings a
  bove (0.5 CPU / 1G backend, 0.25 CPU / 512M frontend) are sized conservatively for demo usage.

                                                                                                              
