• Session restoration in Bob Shell works through the checkpointing system. Checkpoints are automatically crea
  ted whenever you approve a file-modifying operation.

  To list available checkpoints for this project, run:

  /restore

  This shows all saved checkpoints with names in the format:

  2025-06-22T10-00-00_000Z-my-file.txt-write_file

  To restore a specific checkpoint:

  /restore 2025-06-22T10-00-00_000Z-my-file.txt-write_file

  Restoring a checkpoint will:


  1. Revert your files to their state at that point
  2. Restore the conversation history from that moment
  3. Re-propose the original tool call that was about to run

  | Note: Checkpoints only exist if file-modifying operations were approved in a previous session. If no chec
  kpoints were created, there is nothing to restore.



