  ## Summary of changes

  ### The bug and root cause

  run_workflow was a single linear function that auto-inserted approval records and called sm.advance past bo
  th human gates in one shot. POST /change-requests ran the entire workflow synchronously to DONE.

  ### Fix: run_workflow is now a resumable phase-runner (orchestrator/agent_runner.py (orchestrator/agent_run
  ner.py))

  The function now reads current state and runs only the appropriate segment, then returns:

  ┌───────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────
  │ Current state when called │ Work done                                    │ Stops at                      
  ├───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────
  │ INTAKE                    │ Discovery + Planning agents                  │ COORDINATE
  ├───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────
  │ MODIFY                    │ Modify + Rehearse + Verify + Gate evaluation │ APPROVE (if VERIFIED) or GATE_
  ├───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────
  │ anything else             │ Nothing — returns silently                   │ unchanged
  └───────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────
  [table cropped to terminal width 107]

  run_workflow never writes an approval row. That is exclusively the human's action via POST /approve.

  ### _run_verify_phase advance logic

  GATE_DECISION → APPROVE is now automatic when the gate result is VERIFIED — this is a deterministic machine
   transition, not a human gate. The human gate is APPROVE → DONE only, via legacy_removal approval.

  ### POST /approve in orchestrator/main.py (orchestrator/main.py)


  • coordinate: records approval → advances COORDINATE → MODIFY → calls run_workflow(MODIFY) → change lands a
  t APPROVE → returned as new_status.
  • legacy_removal: calls evaluate_gate() server-side before recording anything; returns 409 if result is NOT
  _PROVEN_SAFE, regardless of what state the change is in.

